{
  "_comment": "Loot pools for inventoryConfig.randomLootContainers. Each tier fills a fixed recipe ('slots') instead of drawing N independent items from one bag: every slot pulls only from its group (weapon/gear/ammo/meds/barter), classified from the item's base class at load time, so a crate reads as a set rather than a smear. A slot with 'chance' rolls for it and falls back to 'fallback' when it misses; slot counts must sum to rewardCount. Attachments are deliberately absent from every pool - WeaponKitPatch fits scope/muzzle/foregrip/tactical to the dropped gun, graded by 'modTier', so loose ones were only ever noise. Ammo spawns as loose tpls (Harmony patch stacks to full); weapons spawn from their default preset. Common=curated scav loot that sells or feeds hideout crafts; Rare=gear-dominant, gun is the treat; Epic=top-end gear + valuable barter. Weight = relative pull chance within a group.",
  "foundInRaid": true,
